---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "../components/Icon.astro";

const updated = "September 9, 2026";
const contactEmail = "robotics-outreach@tawasaw.org";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service | Tawasaw Robotics"
  description="The terms that apply when you use the Tawasaw Robotics Silicon Valley website or submit a program application through it."
>
  <main>
    <div class="subnav">
      <div class="shell subnav__inner">
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/">
          <Icon name="arrow-left" size={18} />
          Return home
        </a>
        <p class="subnav__season">Last updated {updated}</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="shell section__inner page-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          These terms cover this website and the program applications submitted
          through it. They are meant to be readable, not to trap anyone — if
          something here is unclear, email us and ask.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--muted">
      <div class="shell section__inner">
        <div class="policy">
          <h2>The short version</h2>
          <ul class="checklist">
            <li>
              This is an informational site for a youth robotics program. It
              sells nothing and collects no payments.
            </li>
            <li>
              Submitting an application is not enrollment, and it does not
              guarantee a spot on a team.
            </li>
            <li>
              Actually joining a team involves separate paperwork — FIRST
              registration and our own permission forms — and those documents
              control, not this page.
            </li>
            <li>
              Schedules, dates, age ranges, and program details on this site can
              change.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Accepting these terms</h2>
          <p>
            By using <strong>robotics.tawasaw.org</strong> or submitting an
            application through it, you agree to these terms. If you do not
            agree, please do not use the site.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you are under 18, read these terms with a parent or guardian. A
            parent or guardian must be the one to submit an application and to
            agree to these terms on a student's behalf.
          </p>

          <h2>What this site is</h2>
          <p>
            This site describes the Tawasaw Robotics FIRST LEGO League and
            FIRST Tech Challenge programs in Silicon Valley, lists past season
            results, and links to application forms. It is informational.
          </p>
          <p>
            Program details — meeting times, start dates, age and grade ranges,
            application deadlines, and which teams we field — reflect our plans
            at the time of writing and may change as a season develops. Nothing
            on this site is a binding offer of admission, a promise that a
            specific team or program will run, or a guarantee that a student
            will compete at any particular event.
          </p>

          <h2>Applying to a program</h2>
          <p>When you submit an application form, you agree that:</p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              You are the student's parent or legal guardian, or you are
              submitting with their permission.
            </li>
            <li>
              The information you provide is accurate and current, and you will
              tell us if it changes.
            </li>
            <li>
              Submitting an application starts a conversation. It is not
              acceptance, enrollment, or a reserved spot.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Space on our teams is limited. We may decline an application, close
            a program early, place a student on a waitlist, or assign a student
            to a different team than the one requested. FIRST sets its own
            eligibility rules for each program, and those rules apply regardless
            of what an application says.
          </p>

          <h2>Participation is governed separately</h2>
          <p>
            These terms cover the website. They do not govern participation in a
            program. Joining a team requires separate documents, which may
            include registration and consent forms through FIRST, our own
            permission and media forms, a team code of conduct, and any
            arrangements for fees, travel, or equipment.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>
              Where those documents and this page disagree, those documents
              control.
            </strong>
          </p>

          <h2>No payments through this site</h2>
          <p>
            This site does not process payments, take donations, or store
            payment information, and no page here asks for a card number. If any
            program fee or trip cost applies, we communicate it directly to
            families and handle it outside this website. Treat any page or
            message that asks you to pay Tawasaw Robotics through this site as
            fraudulent, and please tell us about it.
          </p>

          <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
          <p>When using this site, please do not:</p>
          <ul class="bullets">
            <li>
              Submit false information, or apply on behalf of a child you are
              not responsible for.
            </li>
            <li>
              Submit content that is unlawful, harassing, hateful, or otherwise
              inappropriate for a program serving children.
            </li>
            <li>
              Attempt to break, probe, overload, or gain unauthorized access to
              the site or the services behind it.
            </li>
            <li>
              Scrape or reuse the site's content or images for commercial
              purposes without our permission.
            </li>
            <li>
              Use the site to contact our students or families for advertising
              or solicitation.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <h2>Content and intellectual property</h2>
          <p>
            The text, images, photographs, logos, and design on this site belong
            to Tawasaw Robotics or are used with permission, and are not
            licensed for reuse. You are welcome to link to this site, quote
            short passages with attribution, and share our public posts.
          </p>
          <p>
            The source code for this website is a separate matter: it is
            published on GitHub under the BSD 2-Clause License, and that license
            governs the code alone. It does not grant any right to our name,
            logos, photographs, or written content.
          </p>
          <p>
            FIRST, FIRST LEGO League, and FIRST Tech Challenge are trademarks of
            For Inspiration and Recognition of Science and Technology (FIRST).
            LEGO is a trademark of the LEGO Group. Both are used here only to
            identify the programs our teams participate in. Neither organization
            sponsors, authorizes, or endorses this site.
          </p>

          <h2>Third-party services and links</h2>
          <p>
            Our application pages embed Google Forms, and the site links out to
            Instagram, YouTube, the Tawasaw Institute site, and a separate team
            site for FTC #30619. Those services and sites are run by other
            people under their own terms and privacy policies. We do not control
            them and are not responsible for their content, availability, or
            practices.
          </p>

          <h2>Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            Our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> explains what we collect
            through this site and how we handle it, including information about
            children. It is part of these terms.
          </p>

          <h2>Availability and accuracy</h2>
          <p>
            This site is provided as is and as available. We work to keep it
            accurate and online, but we do not guarantee that it will be
            uninterrupted, error-free, or current at every moment, and we may
            change or remove any part of it at any time. To the fullest extent
            allowed by law, we disclaim implied warranties of merchantability,
            fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
          </p>

          <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent allowed by law, Tawasaw Robotics and its
            coaches, mentors, volunteers, and staff are not liable for indirect,
            incidental, or consequential damages arising from your use of this
            website, or from reliance on information published here that later
            changed.
          </p>
          <p>
            Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under
            law, and nothing here affects the separate agreements and releases
            that govern actual program participation.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
          <p>
            We may update these terms. When we do, we will revise the page and
            the "last updated" date at the top. Continuing to use the site after
            a change means you accept the updated terms.
          </p>

          <h2>Governing law</h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by the laws of the State of California,
            without regard to its conflict-of-laws rules. Any dispute about this
            website will be handled in the state or federal courts located in
            Santa Clara County, California.
          </p>

          <h2>Contact us</h2>
          <p>
            Questions about these terms:
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.
          </p>
          <p class="policy__updated">Last updated {updated}.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
